WEBVTT

00:07:59.538 --> 00:08:01.913
you have a better chance of
making a great movie.

00:08:01.913 --> 00:08:03.246
And if you make a great movie,

00:08:03.246 --> 00:08:05.746
you have a better chance of
making a profitable one.

00:08:06.496 --> 00:08:09.329
And so, you know, I think that that's

00:08:09.329 --> 00:08:11.496
a lesson that everybody
instinctively knows.

00:08:11.871 --> 00:08:14.329
But it's not one that has been
the guiding principle of

00:08:14.329 --> 00:08:16.746
the film industry for a very
long time, if ever.

00:08:17.538 --> 00:08:20.538
So they've kind of worked both
artistically and profitably.

00:08:21.038 --> 00:08:25.121
What lessons do you think you've learned
that apply to people who don't work

00:08:25.121 --> 00:08:27.704
in entertainment or maybe even
in a creative field at all?

00:08:27.704 --> 00:08:32.037
Because it seems like so much of what
you've learned here is that challenging